In Tailwind v4, use the `@custom-variant` directive in your CSS (no config.js needed):

```css
@custom-variant pwa (@media (display-mode: standalone));
```

Then use it like: `<button className='mb-2 md:mb-4 pwa:mb-6 ...' />`

For multi-rule/nested cases (e.g. combining with `&`), see the nested form example. Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx` § "Adding custom variants" (also documented in `src/docs/hover-focus-and-other-states.mdx` § "Registering a custom variant").

